  "rationale": "Direct-match candidates are present (multiple models with trait_efo = obstructive sleep apnea / sleep apnea). PGS005219 is the best-supported choice from the visible metadata because it is explicitly aligned to obstructive sleep apnea, uses a multi-score aggregation-style method (\"weighted PRSsummation PRS-CSs\") with ~983k variants (structurally strong), is developed across multiple cohorts (FinnGen, MGBB, MVP), and reports strong effect-size evidence (OR=1.98, 95% CI 1.74–2.24) plus AUROC=0.79 in validation (n=21,975). However, confidence is not High because the reported performance appears to be full-model AUROC and the model includes BMI adjustment context (AdjustedBMI) and BMI in covariates, which reduces comparability to PRS-only performance; additionally, another closely related sibling (PGS005220) has similar structure and performance, leaving some within-family ambiguity."
