{
  "outcome": "DIRECT_SUB_OPTIMAL",
  "best_model_id": "PGS005217",
  "confidence": "Moderate",
  "rationale": "All four candidates are broadly aligned to the target concept of peripheral vascular disease, but two are explicitly for peripheral artery disease (PGS005158, PGS005217) and two are “peripheral vascular disease, unspecified” from a portability framework (PGS001843, PGS002055). PGS005217 is best supported because it is a disease-focused PAD score with a modern genome-wide shrinkage method (LDpred2), very large variant count (1,296,292), multi-ancestry evaluation, and a strong reported per-SD effect size (HR=1.66) plus a reported C-index (0.731). The main limitation is imperfect phenotype alignment to the broader target label (PAD is a subtype within peripheral vascular disease) and the remaining candidates include exact-label ‘unspecified’ PVD scores, but those are from a pan-trait portability study with only weak PRS-comparable partial correlations (~0.015–0.018) and no AUC/R2, leaving some residual uncertainty about the best direct match for a broad PVD definition."
}

