  "rationale": "All four candidates are direct matches at the disease-family level for the target (peripheral vascular disease), but they split between an exact-label \"peripheral vascular disease, unspecified\" (PGS001843, PGS002055) and the closely related/overlapping clinical entity \"peripheral artery/arterial disease\" (PGS005158, PGS005217). Among them, PGS005217 is best supported by a combination of (i) endpoint fidelity via phenotyping_reported = \"Incident peripheral artery disease\" (a direct clinical endpoint rather than an unspecified umbrella label), (ii) method/structure strength (LDpred2 with ~1.3M variants, consistent with genome-wide shrinkage and high polygenic signal capture), and (iii) stronger PRS-relevant effect-size evidence (HR=1.66 per SD) plus a reported concordance statistic (C-index=0.731, though this is a full-model metric). The main limitation is imperfect phenotype alignment to the target wording (PAD vs unspecified PVD) and that the exact-label UKB portability models (PGS001843/PGS002055) provide only weak PRS-comparable evidence (partial-r ~0.015–0.018) with no AUC/R2, making the overall direct-match selection evidence incomplete rather than decisively high-quality."
}

